;; Package x509 implements a subset of the X.509 standard.
;;
;; It allows parsing and generating certificates, certificate signing
;; requests, certificate revocation lists, and encoded public and private keys.
;; It provides a certificate verifier, complete with a chain builder.
;;
;; The package targets the X.509 technical profile defined by the IETF (RFC
;; 2459/3280/5280), and as further restricted by the CA/Browser Forum Baseline
;; Requirements. There is minimal support for features outside of these
;; profiles, as the primary goal of the package is to provide compatibility
;; with the publicly trusted TLS certificate ecosystem and its policies and
;; constraints.
;;
;; On macOS and Windows, certificate verification is handled by system APIs, but
;; the package aims to apply consistent validation rules across operating
;; systems.
(in-ns 'go.crypto.x509) (go/file "x509.go" :doc "Package x509 implements a subset of the X.509 standard.\n\nIt allows parsing and generating certificates, certificate signing\nrequests, certificate revocation lists, and encoded public and private keys.\nIt provides a certificate verifier, complete with a chain builder.\n\nThe package targets the X.509 technical profile defined by the IETF (RFC\n2459/3280/5280), and as further restricted by the CA/Browser Forum Baseline\nRequirements. There is minimal support for features outside of these\nprofiles, as the primary goal of the package is to provide compatibility\nwith the publicly trusted TLS certificate ecosystem and its policies and\nconstraints.\n\nOn macOS and Windows, certificate verification is handled by system APIs, but\nthe package aims to apply consistent validation rules across operating\nsystems.\n" :imports [


